From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: xiaomi-n1: add stock 120 Hz full-modeset support

Expose 60 and 120 Hz, retaining 60 Hz as preferred. Select the incoming
connector/CRTC mode during prepare, as in the NT36532E driver. An unknown
active mode is an error rather than silently initializing the wrong rate.

Use the current Aurora stock FDT initialization for each rate. Factor
common command ranges, preserving packet types, LP state, delays and all
122 commands at 60 Hz. At 120 Hz send the extra OSC writes and its own
26/2f/BC rate selection, omitting the 60 Hz BA sequence (121 commands).
Both sequences initialize flat mode on; there is no new userspace flat
mode control or seamless timing-switch path.

Keep the OEM 1.36 GHz lane budget at both refresh rates: at 120 Hz the
compressed horizontal total is 466 and DRM htotal is 1522. Doubling the
corrected 60 Hz clock would overclock the DSI link. DSC/PPS and power
sequencing remain unchanged. Mode changes use full panel power cycles.

Official Android U reference (older init revision; data here is from the
newer stock Aurora FDT, not copied wholesale from the Android driver):
https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_qcom_proprietary_display-devicetree/blob/3354864add728de1916f65511c25a512e8b06a72/display/dsi-panel-n1-42-02-0a-dsc-cmd.dtsi
https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_opensource_display-drivers/blob/828d8a4fa074706bf087c5a22152309d29ea15c2/msm/mi_disp/mi_dsi_panel.c

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
